\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces The full crossing funnel: every one of the 20 windows, of 431{}, containing a $\geq 5\sigma $ crossing at the propagated stellar position, ordered by $T_\star $. `Ring max' is the largest of that window's 512{} control statistics, and a window is control-ring exceedance (bold, four of the 20) when $T_\star $ exceeds it. $\Delta \nu $ and $\Delta v$ are the offsets of the crossing from the nearest catalogued transition of the eight masked species, topocentric; the $\pm 50$\,km\,s$^{-1}$ mask applies in the stellar frame after the conversion chain of Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:conventions}. $\nu $ is the window centre, not the crossing frequency, so it is not $\Delta \nu $ from the transition. A dash means the released products record no nearest masked transition for that window. ALMA\nobreakspace  {}J1537$-$3319 is ALMA J153702653-33192492 in the released table.}}{31}{table.20}\protected@file@percent }
